      {
        "id": "p4-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "How many perfect squares have four digits?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$68$",
          "worked": "$31^2=961$ and $32^2=1024$, so the first four-digit perfect square is $32^2$. Also, $99^2=9801$ and $100^2=10000$, so the last is $99^2$.\n\nThe bases are the integers from $32$ to $99$ inclusive. The number of four-digit perfect squares is\n$$99-32+1=68.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "How many perfect cubes have four digits?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$12$",
          "worked": "$9^3=729$ and $10^3=1000$, so the first four-digit perfect cube is $10^3$. Also, $21^3=9261$ and $22^3=10648$, so the last is $21^3$.\n\nThe bases are the integers from $10$ to $21$ inclusive. The number of four-digit perfect cubes is\n$$21-10+1=12.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
  },
